// REJECTED — G4: a host acquisition in a `fn` body a component reaches.
//
// `Pool.open` opens a host resource whose release is a separate verb, and only
// an acquisition bracket (`effect <acquire> undo <release>`) registers that
// release with the activation's teardown accumulator. A `fn` body has no
// bracket, so the pool is opened per call and never closed — the runtime
// reports `pool#1 (open() with no close())` (R1) on a program the checker
// admitted.
//
// The reach qualifier is the invariant: residue is defined against an
// ACTIVATION, which promises that teardown releases everything it acquired. A
// helper the activation calls acquires inside that promise while contributing
// nothing to it. A `pub fn` no component reaches is a library entry point whose
// lifecycle belongs to the foreign caller, and revl promises nothing about it.
//
// expected error:
//   host acquisition `Pool.open` cannot be called in `fn open_it`, which a
//     component body reaches — nothing registers its `close()`, so the
//     resource is acquired irreversibly (G4)

fn open_it(u: Str) -> Int {
  let p = Pool.open(u, 1)
  return 1
}

service S { fn go(u: Str) -> Int }

component C provides s: S {
  provide s { fn go(u) = open_it(u) }
}
